{"name":"October","hex":"#c67533","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"October","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The tenth month of the Gregorian calendar, following September and preceding November.","A female given name transferred from the month name."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of ale traditionally brewed in October. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/October"}],"entries":[{"title":"October","blocks":[{"text":"October is the 10th month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days. The eighth month in the old calendar of Romulus c. 750 BC, October retained its name after January and February were inserted into the calendar that had originally been created by the Romans. In Ancient Rome, one of three Mundus patet would take place on October 5, Meditrinalia October 11, Augustalia on October 12, October Horse on October 15, and Armilustrium on October 19. These dates do not correspond to the modern Gregorian calendar. Among the Anglo-Saxons, it was known as Winterfylleth (Ƿinterfylleþ), because at this full moon, winter was supposed to begin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Snowy_Russian_Street.jpg/330px-Snowy_Russian_Street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October","wikidata":"Q124"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg/500px-Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg/1280px-Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg/500px-Calendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The calendula","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalendula_January_2008-1_filtered.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Opal_Armband_800pix.jpg/500px-Opal_Armband_800pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Opal_Armband_800pix.jpg/500px-Opal_Armband_800pix.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An opal armband. Opal is the birthstone for October.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOpal_Armband_800pix.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Tourmaline_cut.JPG/330px-Tourmaline_cut.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Tourmaline_cut.JPG/330px-Tourmaline_cut.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cut tourmaline","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATourmaline_cut.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Beata_Vergine_Maria%2C_Madonna_del_Rosario.jpg/500px-Beata_Vergine_Maria%2C_Madonna_del_Rosario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Beata_Vergine_Maria%2C_Madonna_del_Rosario.jpg/1280px-Beata_Vergine_Maria%2C_Madonna_del_Rosario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Beata_Vergine_Maria%2C_Madonna_del_Rosario.jpg/500px-Beata_Vergine_Maria%2C_Madonna_del_Rosario.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Our Lady of the Most Holy Rosary, whose devotion and Feast are celebrated in Oct